      "blocks": {
        "card_MxYb3t": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "num": "01",
            "title": "The disease progresses silently",
            "body": "<p>Periodontal disease destroys bone and tissue over years — almost entirely without pain — until the damage is severe enough to cause tooth loss. Silent diseases don't generate alarm. They accumulate in statistics.</p>"
          }
        },
        "card_F8NVTQ": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "num": "03",
            "title": "The mouth is professionally separated fromthe body",
            "body": "<p>Dentistry sits in a separate system — different training, different buildings, different insurance. The documented links to cardiovascular disease, neurodegeneration, diabetes, and pregnancy outcomes are not crossing the disciplinary boundary.</p>"
          }
        },
        "card_EGeHa4": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "num": "02",
            "title": "It is worst where voices are least heard",
            "body": "<p>The communities most affected have the least political voice, least media representation, and least research funding. The invisibility of the crisis mirrors the invisibility of the people it affects most.</p>"
          }
        },
        "card_cTP7ak": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "num": "04",
            "title": "The industry profits from the wrong solution",
            "body": "<p>A $50B+ oral care industry built on the antiseptic paradigm has no structural incentive to question it. The ecological understanding of oral health — which OG3™ is built on — represents a fundamental disruption to a very established business model.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
